Done. Here's what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — Implemented `require_api_key`: reads `X-API-Key`, validates against `VALID_API_KEYS` in `database.py`, and raises HTTP 401 if missing or invalid. Returns the associated username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — Added the remaining endpoints and enhanced `GET /tasks`:

- **`GET /tasks`** — Added optional query params `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (combinable) and `page`/`page_size` (defaults 1/20). Applies filters, then slices the result set.
- **`POST /tasks`** — Requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` against `projects`; returns 404 if absent. Auto-generates the next unique integer ID and appends the new `Task`.
- **`PUT /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Performs partial updates using `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` so only provided fields change. Returns 404 if the task doesn't exist.
- **`DELETE /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Removes the task and returns 204; 404 if not found.

All endpoints were exercised with an inline test script: auth rejection, filtering, pagination, create/update/delete flows, and 404 cases all pass.
